        <field>Body__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">A Japanese pastor who, at 21, moved into the slums of Kobe and lived there. From there he organized labour unions and cooperatives. One of the co-ops he helped start in 1921 is now Co-op Kobe, with about 1.7 million members. In Japan he is still called the father of the co-op movement.</value>
